An unbind that settles a waiting lender but not the borrower it lends to.
The borrower keeps the queue the lender's old units gave it.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a place waits on another queue than its virtual time says
Witness: fuzz lend-revoke-takes-lender

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -677,7 +677,7 @@ void sched_unbind(struct cap *bound)
     }
     *bound = (struct cap){ 0 };
     /* An empty place holds no time, so settling takes it off its queue. */
-    lender_settle(t);
+    thread_settle(t);
 }
 
